    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586-a3">

                <pb facs="0661" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg581"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrios to Mr.
                            Bailey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honorable Sir</hi>: Referring to the esteemed note of
                    your excellency addressed to this office on the 6th ultimo, and adding to the
                    reply to said note sent to your legation on the 12th ultimo, I now have the
                    honor to manifest to your excellency that <pb facs="0662" n="582" xml:id="pg582"
                    /> the Government of Guatemala willingly assents to the reservation which the
                    Government of the United States makes of its right to claim for American
                    creditors benefits equal to those that may be acquired by the citizens of other
                    countries in the adjustment of the foreign debt of the Republic of Guatemala,
                    the Government which I represent being in duty bound to accept such reservation
                    in recognition of the friendly attitude which the United States has always
                    assumed toward Guatemala.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Barrios, M.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
